// boxcxx — <__bits/version_containers>
//
// The __cpp_lib_* feature-test macros [version.syn] owned JOINTLY by the
// container family -- <vector>, <deque>, <list>, <forward_list>, <map>,
// <set>, <unordered_map>, <unordered_set>, <string>, <stack>, <queue> --
// plus <memory>, which shares ownership of
// __cpp_lib_allocator_traits_is_always_equal. Split out for the same
// [support.limits.general] per-header reason as
// <__bits/version_ranges>/<__bits/version_algorithm>/<__bits/version_numeric>
// -- see those files' comments. Every owning header includes this leaf
// directly so each macro is visible from a TU that includes only one of
// them, not just from <version>.
//
// Like <__bits/version_iostreams>, this is one leaf for a family whose
// members do not all own every macro in it: a header here may expose a
// macro it does not itself own. Every macro exposed is nevertheless true
// of boxcxx as a whole, and <version> exposes all of them anyway.
//
// map_try_emplace and unordered_map_try_emplace are P0083R3's try_emplace +
// insert_or_assign. Both were withheld on missing overloads rather than
// missing functions: map had two of the four of each, and unordered_map had
// two of try_emplace and ONE of insert_or_assign -- so an rvalue key was
// copied instead of moved, silently, which is the entire reason that overload
// exists. Ф31e-f completed both sets.
//
// Deliberately absent (see <version>'s list): constexpr_vector,
// constexpr_string.
//
// Every block below is gated on BOXCXX_OWNS_<stem>, and this file has NO
// include guard: it is meant to be included once per owning header, each time
// defining only what that header declared it owns. [support.limits.general]
// says a macro is defined by <version> AND by the header that provides the
// feature; it does not say every header that happens to include this leaf.
// A header that answers for a feature it does not provide is answering a
// question it was not asked, so it no longer does. <version> defines
// BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL and takes the lot. Checked by tools/cxx_ftm_audit.sh.

